request_text:
security: Demographic.java::getStandardIdentificationHTML() appends title, sex, gender without HTML encoding; uses legacy Encode.forHtml() instead of CARLOS wrapper

## Summary

`Demographic.getStandardIdentificationHTML()` (lines 1755–1912) builds an HTML identification block for patient records. Several fields are appended without any encoding, and the fields that are encoded use the legacy `Encode.forHtml()` static call (null-unsafe, banned by CI) instead of the CARLOS `SafeEncode` wrapper.

## Type
Security

## Priority
2-High — Unencoded PHI fields in a shared HTML-building method propagate XSS to every caller; null-unsafe `Encode.forHtml()` can silently emit the literal string `"null"` for missing data, corrupting output.

## Kind
Task

## Affected File

`src/main/java/io/github/carlos_emr/carlos/commn/model/Demographic.java`

## Unencoded Fields

```java
// Line 1768 — title unencoded
sb.append(getTitle() + " ");

// Line 1792 — sex unencoded
sb.append(getSex());

// Line 1802 — gender unencoded
sb.append(getGender());
```

## Legacy Null-Unsafe Encoder Usage

```java
// Lines 1782, 1833–1837 etc. — legacy Encode.forHtml() calls
sb.append(Encode.forHtml(getLastName()));
sb.append(Encode.forHtml(getFirstName()));
sb.append(Encode.forHtml(getHin()));
```

`Encode.forHtml(null)` returns the literal string `"null"` rather than an empty string. This causes visible corruption wherever any nullable demographic field is absent. The CARLOS `SafeEncode.forHtmlContent()` wrapper coalesces null to empty before delegating to OWASP.

CI (`scripts/lint/check-encoder-null-safety.sh`) will fail on these usages.

## Suggested Fix

### Unencoded fields — add encoding

```java
// Before
sb.append(getTitle() + " ");

// After
import io.github.carlos_emr.carlos.utility.SafeEncode;
sb.append(SafeEncode.forHtmlContent(getTitle())).append(" ");
```

Apply the same fix to `getSex()` and `getGender()`.

### Legacy Encode calls — replace with SafeEncode

```java
// Before
sb.append(Encode.forHtml(getLastName()));

// After
sb.append(SafeEncode.forHtmlContent(getLastName()));
```

Replace all `Encode.forHtml(...)` calls in the method with `SafeEncode.forHtmlContent(...)`.

## References

- CLAUDE.md — OWASP Encoding section; CARLOS null-safe wrapper required; CI enforces via `check-encoder-null-safety.sh`
- `src/main/java/io/github/carlos_emr/carlos/utility/SafeEncode.java` — null-safe replacement
- carlos-emr/carlos#2416, carlos-emr/carlos#2417 — same unencoded PHI pattern in edit JSPs

🤖 Generated with <a href="https://claude.com/claude-code">Claude Code</a>

