request_text:
security: TOTP MFA validation has no used-code tracking — same code reusable within ±90s window (claude assist)

## Problem

`isValidTotpCode()` in `Login2Action` accepts any code matching the current, previous, or next 30-second TOTP time step (±1 step, ≈90-second window), but does not track previously accepted codes. A code that has already been used to authenticate can be accepted again within the same window.

```java
// src/main/java/io/github/carlos_emr/carlos/login/Login2Action.java:918–935
private boolean isValidTotpCode(String mfaSecret, String submittedCode) throws InvalidKeyException {
    // ... setup ...
    return constantTimeEquals(totpGenerator.generateOneTimePasswordString(key, now), submittedCode)
            || constantTimeEquals(totpGenerator.generateOneTimePasswordString(key, now.minus(timeStep)), submittedCode)
            || constantTimeEquals(totpGenerator.generateOneTimePasswordString(key, now.plus(timeStep)), submittedCode);
    // No recording of accepted codes.
}
```

**Exploit scenario** (requires multiple prior factors):

1. Attacker obtains valid credentials (username + password + PIN) by some prior means.
2. Attacker observes or intercepts a valid TOTP code the legitimate user just submitted (shoulder surfing, phishing proxy, network interception before TLS).
3. Within the same ≈90-second window, the attacker submits the same code from a different IP/session that already has its own fresh pending-MFA challenge token.
4. Authentication succeeds.

The pending-MFA challenge token is per-session and consumed on first use, so the attacker must independently complete password+PIN validation first. This is a realistic multi-step attack in a healthcare threat model.

## Suggested fix

Maintain a short-lived cache keyed by provider security ID, mapping to the set of recently accepted codes. Before accepting a code, check the cache; after accepting, insert it.

```java
// Pseudocode addition to Login2Action or a new MfaUsedCodeCache helper
private static final Cache<Integer, Set<String>> USED_TOTP_CODES = Caffeine.newBuilder()
        .expireAfterWrite(Duration.ofSeconds(90))
        .build();

private boolean isValidTotpCode(String mfaSecret, String submittedCode, int securityNo)
        throws InvalidKeyException {
    boolean valid = /* existing three-step check */;
    if (valid) {
        Set<String> used = USED_TOTP_CODES.get(securityNo, k -> ConcurrentHashMap.newKeySet());
        if (!used.add(submittedCode)) {
            return false; // replay detected
        }
    }
    return valid;
}
```

The Caffeine dependency is already present in the project.

## References

- `src/main/java/io/github/carlos_emr/carlos/login/Login2Action.java:918–935` (`isValidTotpCode`)
- `src/main/java/io/github/carlos_emr/carlos/login/Login2Action.java:816–826` (call site in `validateMfaAndCompleteLogin`)
- RFC 6238 §5.2 recommends token-use tracking to prevent replay attacks

🤖 Generated with <a href="https://claude.com/claude-code">Claude Code</a>

