&gt; Rejects any non-`http:`/`https:` protocol	✅
&gt; Allows `https://` for any hostname (OpenAI, Azure, OpenRouter, custom)	✅
&gt; Allows `http://localhost`	✅
&gt; Allows `http://127.0.0.1`	✅
&gt; Allows `http://[::1]` (IPv6 loopback with bracket handling)	✅
&gt; `LOCALHOST` (uppercased) → allowed via `.toLowerCase()`	✅
&gt; `localhost.` (trailing dot) → **rejected** (≠ `localhost`) — conservative but correct	✅
&gt; `localhost.evil.com` → rejected (full hostname comparison, not prefix)	✅
&gt; `127.0.0.1.evil.com` → rejected	✅
&gt; `http://192.168.1.1` → rejected	✅
&gt; `http://0.0.0.0` → rejected	✅
&gt; `http://169.254.169.254` → rejected	✅
&gt; `http://[::ffff:127.0.0.1]` → bracket-stripped to `::ffff:127.0.0.1` ≠ `::1` → rejected	✅
&gt; `http://[fe80::1]` → bracket-stripped to `fe80::1` ≠ `::1` → rejected	✅
&gt; `http://0177.0.0.1` → WHATWG URL normalizes to `127.0.0.1` → **allowed** (correct — it IS loopback)	✅
&gt; `http://2130706433` (decimal IPv4 for 127.0.0.1) → WHATWG normalizes → **allowed** (correct)	✅
&gt; Backslash/encoded-host spoofing not possible — `new URL()` normalizes before comparison	✅
&gt; Does not echo credentials in errors	⚠️ See credential leakage finding above
&gt; The IPv6 bracket-stripping logic (`parsed.hostname.toLowerCase().replace(/^\[|\]$/g, '')`) correctly handles Node's WHATWG URL representation where `http://[::1]/v1` yields `hostname = "[::1]"`.
&gt; 
&gt; ### callLLM integration assessment
&gt; `validateLLMBaseUrl(config.baseUrl)` appears at **line 173**, which is the very first executable statement in `callLLM()` — before message construction, provider detection (`azure` flag), URL building (`buildRequestUrl`), auth header construction, the retry loop, and all `fetch()` calls. The validation is unconditional and not gated on provider type. All paths through `callLLM()` — non-streaming JSON response and streaming SSE — are covered because both use the same `url` from `buildRequestUrl(config.baseUrl, ...)`, and that call is also after validation. Azure content-filter handling, rate-limit retry, and network-error retry paths are all within the retry loop, which is entered only after validation passes. **No fetch-before-validation path exists.**
&gt; 
&gt; ### Backend URL / CSRF assessment
